1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,956
Last time you wrote for the admiral's seat, in a lab.

2
00:00:04,856 --> 00:00:06,386
Today that seat comes home.

3
00:00:08,186 --> 00:00:10,754
Your universe gets a second way to play,

4
00:00:11,204 --> 00:00:12,543
right beside the bridge crew.

5
00:00:13,443 --> 00:00:15,975
And here's the part that matters most to a writer.

6
00:00:16,875 --> 00:00:18,634
If nobody wants that chair,

7
00:00:19,084 --> 00:00:21,226
the crew's evening doesn't change at all.

8
00:00:22,426 --> 00:00:25,520
A campaign has no admiral unless you ask for one.

9
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:28,556
And you ask by writing chapters.

10
00:00:30,356 --> 00:00:32,234
Three things have to be true.

11
00:00:33,134 --> 00:00:35,251
The admiral's library is loaded.

12
00:00:36,151 --> 00:00:40,379
The mode is campaign, with an admiralty chapter in your own file.

13
00:00:41,279 --> 00:00:44,401
And there's a worldlets chapter with a world in it.

14
00:00:46,201 --> 00:00:48,495
I left each one out in turn, and played it.

15
00:00:49,395 --> 00:00:53,240
Every time, no console, no world, and empty pools.

16
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:57,005
So the chapters are the switch.

17
00:00:58,205 --> 00:01:01,164
First, I look in one file I never edit.

18
00:01:02,064 --> 00:01:05,061
Story dot json is the list of libraries.

19
00:01:05,961 --> 00:01:08,582
The last two lines are the universe's own,

20
00:01:09,032 --> 00:01:10,065
and then the admiral's.

21
00:01:11,865 --> 00:01:14,175
If yours has both, leave it alone.

22
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,219
That line does nothing by itself.

23
00:01:19,019 --> 00:01:19,935
Now for the mode.

24
00:01:20,835 --> 00:01:23,954
One word changes, from story to campaign.

25
00:01:24,854 --> 00:01:27,681
For the crew, that's all it is: a word.

26
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:30,808
Now the four chapters from the lab.

27
00:01:31,708 --> 00:01:33,816
They go at the very end of the file,

28
00:01:34,266 --> 00:01:35,860
so nothing above them moves.

29
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,308
There are two worlds:

30
00:01:39,758 --> 00:01:44,287
Hollin Prime, which never runs dry, and the Lamp, which does.

31
00:01:46,087 --> 00:01:48,713
An admiralty chapter with two dials.

32
00:01:49,613 --> 00:01:51,546
One officer, Commodore Maren.

33
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:54,740
And a ladder of two research steps.

34
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:59,753
The Compact's home is the system every game starts in.

35
00:02:00,653 --> 00:02:02,068
It still gets its world,

36
00:02:02,518 --> 00:02:04,932
and it's the first one that says unlimited.

37
00:02:06,132 --> 00:02:09,496
Now, the numbers, and I'll be straight with you.

38
00:02:10,396 --> 00:02:12,896
I wrote nothing for starting ore,

39
00:02:13,346 --> 00:02:16,223
so the game used its own three hundred.

40
00:02:17,123 --> 00:02:20,063
And it started with three thousand six hundred.

41
00:02:21,863 --> 00:02:24,885
Part of that is the pace, which is yours to set.

42
00:02:25,785 --> 00:02:29,430
Most of it is a test setting the game's makers left on.

43
00:02:30,330 --> 00:02:34,093
It multiplies every stock and every yield by eight.

44
00:02:35,893 --> 00:02:37,779
Research isn't multiplied at all.

45
00:02:38,679 --> 00:02:42,439
So for now, the ladder is cheap and the tanks are huge.

46
00:02:44,239 --> 00:02:45,864
Don't balance anything yet.

47
00:02:46,764 --> 00:02:49,289
Just never start with less than a headquarters costs.

48
00:02:50,489 --> 00:02:52,353
I save, and I run lint.

49
00:02:53,253 --> 00:02:55,995
All six files are clean, as they were before.

50
00:02:56,895 --> 00:02:58,858
The four new chapters add no warning.

51
00:03:00,058 --> 00:03:02,062
Now let's play it with both seats filled.

52
00:03:03,862 --> 00:03:06,726
The admiral sees one world at home, and it's mine.

53
00:03:07,626 --> 00:03:08,878
I build a headquarters.

54
00:03:09,328 --> 00:03:10,875
It takes about half a minute.

55
00:03:12,675 --> 00:03:16,569
Then an extractor, an academy, a shipyard and a lab.

56
00:03:17,469 --> 00:03:19,697
The ore starts to climb.

57
00:03:21,497 --> 00:03:23,432
The shipyard offers Commodore Maren,

58
00:03:23,882 --> 00:03:25,389
and she brings three ships.

59
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:27,966
The lab offers my first step.

60
00:03:28,416 --> 00:03:30,458
Forty seconds later, it's done,

61
00:03:30,908 --> 00:03:32,629
and it offers the second.

62
00:03:34,429 --> 00:03:35,878
And over on the bridge?

63
00:03:36,778 --> 00:03:39,270
Five hundred credits, and three leads.

64
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,277
Nothing at all has changed.

65
00:03:42,477 --> 00:03:44,467
Now the question you should ask first.

66
00:03:45,367 --> 00:03:48,205
What does this cost a table that doesn't want an admiral?

67
00:03:50,005 --> 00:03:51,916
So I walked the whole capstone evening,

68
00:03:52,366 --> 00:03:55,925
with these chapters in the file and that chair empty.

69
00:03:57,725 --> 00:03:59,269
Every row came out the same.

70
00:04:00,169 --> 00:04:02,534
The world is there, as scenery.

71
00:04:02,984 --> 00:04:05,678
The pools sit full, and never move.

72
00:04:07,478 --> 00:04:10,650
So you can ship one universe to both kinds of table.

73
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:12,821
How does it end?

74
00:04:13,721 --> 00:04:16,102
The admiral's game has no ending of its own here.

75
00:04:17,002 --> 00:04:20,619
The campaign ends where your goals chapter says.

76
00:04:21,069 --> 00:04:22,671
That's your win line.

77
00:04:24,471 --> 00:04:26,189
And when I stop and continue?

78
00:04:27,089 --> 00:04:29,108
The pools come back, to the last unit.

79
00:04:30,008 --> 00:04:32,114
So do all five platforms,

80
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:34,532
the fleet, and the research.

81
00:04:36,332 --> 00:04:39,304
Twenty seconds in, the extractor's working again.

82
00:04:40,504 --> 00:04:41,506
Now it's your turn.

83
00:04:42,406 --> 00:04:44,908
Write your own home world, two officers,

84
00:04:45,358 --> 00:04:47,160
and a ladder of three steps.

85
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:52,069
Then take the admiral out, by changing one key,

86
00:04:52,519 --> 00:04:54,934
and check the crew's game is the same.

87
00:04:55,834 --> 00:04:56,919
Then put it back,

88
00:04:57,369 --> 00:04:59,279
and hand that chair to a friend.

89
00:05:01,079 --> 00:05:03,220
Next time is the capstone.

90
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,808
It works with an admiral in the file, or without.
